  "slug": "basal-ganglia-29a7",
  "summary": "Public brain single-cell resources are now being harmonized and paired with imaging and genetic context, making cell-type readouts reusable across studies.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is single-cell and single-nucleus resources that place brain cell types in disease, ageing and genetic context. A harmonized dataset of cortical and hippocampal transcriptomes from wild-type and Alzheimer's disease model mice standardizes sample annotations to make public snRNA-seq reusable. A multi-omic QTL atlas from 231 human prefrontal cortex donors links disorder-associated genetic risk to cell-type and developmental gene regulation. The HypoAD atlas pairs MRI from 458 people with 614,403 snRNA-seq nuclei to relate hypothalamic volume to cell-type changes in ageing and Alzheimer's disease, and scCVD integrates scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq from 701 samples covering over 4.68 million cells. What is new is the pairing of cell-type-resolved transcriptomic or regulatory readouts with imaging, genetic or disease-model context, while tissue focus varies across these studies. Tools such as SCOUBI and VEGABrain extend this toward spatial and developmental interpretation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
